<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="A local engineering showcase for campus-style appointment coordination.">
  <title><%= title || 'IITI Health Centre' %></title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/app.css">
</head>
<body>
<header class="site-header"><div class="site-header-inner">
  <a class="brand" href="/">IITI Health Centre</a>
  <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="#for-patients">For Patients</a><details><summary>For Staff</summary><div class="nav-dropdown"><a href="/login/doctor">Doctor sign in</a><a href="/login/admin">Administrator sign in</a></div></details><a href="#about-demo">About (Demo)</a></nav>
</div></header>
<main>
  <section class="hero page-shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="demo-notice"><span class="demo-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Local demo <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Not a live campus service</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">IITI Health Centre</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">A campus-style appointment coordination system.</p>
      <p class="hero-body">Request care, follow your appointment status, and review visit details recorded by the care team. This local engineering showcase demonstrates how patients, administrators, and doctors coordinate care.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <% if (currentUser) { %>
          <a class="button primary" href="/dashboard">Go to your dashboard</a>
          <% if (currentUser.role === 'patient') { %><a class="button secondary" href="/appointments/new">Request an appointment</a><% } %>
        <% } else { %>
          <a class="button primary" href="/register">Create a patient account</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="/login/patient">Patient sign in</a>
        <% } %>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">For demonstration only. Do not enter real medical or personal information.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="status-register" aria-labelledby="status-title">
      <div class="register-heading"><span class="register-index">01</span><h2 id="status-title">Appointment status</h2></div>
      <p class="register-intro">Each request moves through a clear coordination stage.</p>
      <ol class="status-list">
        <li><span class="status-mark status-requested" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><strong>Requested</strong><p>Waiting for an administrator to review.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="status-mark status-confirmed" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><strong>Confirmed</strong><p>A doctor and appointment time are assigned.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="status-mark status-completed" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><strong>Completed</strong><p>Visit details are available when recorded.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="status-mark status-other" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><strong>Rejected or cancelled</strong><p>The request will not proceed as scheduled.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
      <a class="text-link" href="#how-it-works">See how coordination works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="how-section" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-index">A clear path through care</p><h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2></div><p>One shared workflow keeps each person’s next step easy to understand.</p></div>
      <ol class="steps-list">
        <li><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Patient requests</h3><p>Share a short description and preferred contact details.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Admin coordinates</h3><p>An administrator reviews the request, assigns a doctor, and schedules a time.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Doctor records visit</h3><p>The doctor marks the visit complete and records any follow-up details.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">04</span><h3>Patient follows up</h3><p>Check the latest status and review details recorded for the visit.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="patient-section page-shell" id="for-patients" aria-labelledby="patient-title">
    <div class="patient-copy"><p class="section-index">For patients</p><h2 id="patient-title">Know where your request stands.</h2><p>Create an account to request an appointment and keep its coordination details together. Sign in any time to review the latest status.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="<%= currentUser && currentUser.role === 'patient' ? '/appointments/new' : '/register' %>"><%= currentUser && currentUser.role === 'patient' ? 'Request an appointment' : 'Get started as a patient' %></a><a class="text-link" href="/login/patient">Already registered? Sign in</a></div></div>
    <div class="patient-aside"><h3>What this demo includes</h3><ul><li>Patient account registration and sign-in</li><li>Appointment requests and status tracking</li><li>Staff scheduling and visit documentation</li></ul></div>
  </section>

  <section class="staff-section" id="for-staff" aria-labelledby="staff-title"><div class="page-shell staff-inner"><div><p class="section-index">For care team staff</p><h2 id="staff-title">Coordinate requests in one workspace.</h2><p>Staff accounts are provisioned for this local demonstration. Choose a role to sign in.</p></div><div class="staff-links"><a href="/login/doctor">Doctor sign in <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/login/admin">Administrator sign in <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="demo-section page-shell" id="about-demo" aria-labelledby="demo-title"><div><p class="section-index">About this demonstration</p><h2 id="demo-title">A local-first engineering showcase.</h2></div><div><p>This application demonstrates care-coordination workflows using a local development setup. It is not connected to a campus health service, does not provide medical advice, and is not intended for real patient information.</p><p>Use fictional details when exploring the demo. Notification messages are shown through a local console adapter.</p></div></section>
</main>
<footer class="site-footer"><div class="site-footer-inner"><p>IITI Health Centre · Local engineering showcase</p><p>Not a live campus service. Do not enter real medical information.</p></div></footer>
</body>
</html>
